  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Core", "items": [
      "Filesystem is authoritative; caches are disposable",
      "383 production commands registered in lib.rs; conflicts cross as IpcError { code, message }",
      "save_document: path-transaction admission, write policy, managed-vault check, revision check, managed-root snapshot, then atomic replace",
      "Frontmatter edits go through frontmatter/ops.rs, preserving key order and comments"
    ] },
    { "dot": "violet", "title": "AI and Skills", "items": [
      "ai_router, background skill dispatch and the five-role loop build argv with agent_host::provider; each spawns its own CLI process",
      "Terminal dispatch returns its own launch spec for the embedded PTY; Codex runs via /bin/zsh -lc with shell-quoted args and the prompt in MARU_SKILL_PROMPT",
      "Output returns to the webview as ai://output, ai://done and ai://error events",
      "Adaptive policy is off unless ai.adaptivePolicy is enabled; then agent_host runs dot ai policy resolve --json, and a missing dot or failed resolve stops the launch instead of bypassing permissions",
      "The 60s scheduler ticker dispatches due schedules through the skill host",
      "Bundles from the STAIxBWLB/skills skills-channel release are verified with the updater minisign key"
    ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Integration", "items": [
      "While hub.enabled is false the Hub client still serves the cached catalog and queues submit gates; only HTTP to the Hub is off. Online catalog reads revalidate with ETags",
      "Submit gates pass a safety check (no body, content or binary keys) and queue offline under .maru/queue/hub",
      "maru-mcp is started by an external MCP client over stdio (MARU_MCP_WORKSPACE); the desktop app does not spawn it",
      "The sidecar reads workspace files and only appends proposal events under .maru/runs/skills",
      "The Rust core also runs inbox connectors (gws for Gmail, m365 for Outlook, a configured Python script for Telegram, a KakaoTalk relay folder), the signed Tauri updater, and portable-pty terminal sessions"
    ] }
  ]
